  "reference": "Two half-meter layers, 12 uniform columns, h/dx=0.9. The slab has sinusoidally prescribed wall temperatures, contact resistance 0.32, and distributed heating C dT/dt. Fourier flux is uniform in space. Compare every time sample and all 13 interval-mean section fluxes with the continuous piecewise-linear temperature and exact sinusoidal mean flux across one period.",
  "command": "OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=../TensorSPH/src python examples/sph_fixed_wall_contact_time_order.py",
  "sph_regression": {
    "command": "OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=src:. python -m pytest -q tests/test_conduction_2d.py",
    "passed": 155
  },
  "sdirk2_acceptance": "Record all nine resolutions and require monotonically decreasing temperature, contact flux and all-cut flux errors. Require all three orders above 1.9 on both finest refinements, and column energy residual below 1e-12 J/m2 at every resolution. Early wall flux convergence is slower; worst_cut_x_m and worst_interval_start_s locate the maximum absolute error."
}
